The example of the species-tree window (Tools -> Species Tree from Gene Trees).

genes.tre   40 gene trees on 8 species, A to H, one per line, topologies only. 11 of the genes lack one species.
truth.tre   the species tree they were simulated from.

Made for this project, not taken from any program or data set: a small simulator written for it draws a random species
tree with branch lengths in coalescent units, then a gene tree for each gene under the multispecies coalescent (so that
incomplete lineage sorting makes some genes disagree with the species tree), then drops a random species from some of the
genes. Seed 1 of the simulator's seeds was the first for which the search recovers truth.tre and a branch is not certain.
